<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41345" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιτηδ-εύω</span></b> , impf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπετήδευον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phd.</u>
					64a
				</span></i>
			 : aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπετήδευσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.37
				</span></i>
			 : pf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιτετήδευκα,</span>
			
				Pass.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ευμαι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Hp.Ma.</u>
				304b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				13.65
			</span></i> : (as if a compd. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί,
				Τηδεύω,</span> but it is formed directly from
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιτηδές</span>):—<i>pursue</i> or
				<i>practise</i> a thing, <i>make</i> it <i>one's
			business,</i> c.acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐπαθείας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.135
				</span></i>
			, etc. ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τοῖς κακοῖς..ἀνάγκη κἀπιτηδεύειν
					κακά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					309
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαλιάν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					1069
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐσέβειαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antipho
					2.3.11
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ δ᾽ ἐπὶ κακουργίᾳ καὶ οὐκ ἀρετῇ
					ἐπετήδευσαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.37
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέχνην, μουσικήν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Tht.</u>
				149a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Ath.</u>
				1.13
			</span></i>, etc. ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τι πρός τι</span>
			<i>invent</i> with a view to.., <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				6.125
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be practised,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅσα κακὰ καὶ αἰσχρά τινι
					ἐπιτετήδευται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					13.65
				</span></i>
			 ; also, <i>to be made</i> so and so <i>by art,</i> opp.
			to being so by nature, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.98
			</span></i> ; of dogs, <i>to be carefully trained,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					1.6.40
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c.
			inf.. <i>take care</i> to do, <i>use</i> to do,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				4.170
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				524c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				1.3d
			</span></i>, etc. ; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ὅπως..</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					3.102
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> abs. in
				part., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδὲν αὐτοὶ
				ἐπιτηδεύοντες</span> without any <i>deliberate
			purpose</i> on our part, <i><span class="en">
				Speus.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Theol.Ar.</u>
				61
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιτηδεύσας</span>”
				<i>on purpose,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hld.
					5.31
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
